      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit question: are there any valid ISR values outside the range 0-255 at all? It seems such values are always invalid (and in particular the SVI field in GUEST_INTR_STATUS set to max_isr by `hwapic_isr_update` is only 8 bits)?\n\nIf so, it might make more sense to return -EINVAL in this case, like I suggested earlier?\n\nIn particular, we do this check for both pVM and npVM, and especially for npVM returning -EINVAL seems more appropriate than -EPERM?",
